{"claims":[{"claim_text":"The Declaration of Independence sets forth the fundamental precepts of American government: That God bestows certain inalienable rights on every individual, thus producing human equality; that government exists first and foremost to protect those inalienable rights; that man-made law must be consistent with God-given, natural rights; and that if God-given, natural, inalienable rights come in conflict with government, court, or human-granted rights, God-given, natural, inalienable rights always prevail; that there is a moral law recognized as \"the Laws of Nature and of Nature's God\"; and that American government is to operate with the consent of the governed.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The party identifies as the party of the Declaration of Independence and the Constitution.", "claim_types":["characterization"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Constitution is the greatest political document ever written.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Constitution is a solemn compact built upon principles of the Declaration that enshrines God-given individual rights and ensures that all Americans stand equal before the law.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Constitution defines the purposes and limits of government.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Constitution is the blueprint for ordered liberty that makes the United States the world's freest and most prosperous nation.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

